 "caveats": [
  "Local D002 file = 577,857 cells / 50 donors, subset extraction from collection level (>1M/102) (scope=local empirical); backfilling full collection requires download approval, marked 'pending backfill'.",
  "'Majorclass=Immune Cells' only 1.7%: Ocular surface resident immunity scarce + no immune enrichment step —— Immune proportion cannot be compared against inflammatory disease samples.",
  "published_annotation and majorclass coexist: published_annotation='red blood cells' dominance indicates RBC not cleanly removed from majorclass? No —— majorclass 9 categories contain no RBC class, RBC signals dispersed into various categories, count denominator includes RBC contaminated nuclei, each category % represents 'captured event composition' not tissue ground truth (Astra T2 scope declaration).",
  "Sclera/conjunctiva independent entries see corresponding skeleton files; this entry's corneo-scleral junction layer ≠ independent conjunctival baseline.",
  "v1.1 (KB2c t_be336eee): Primary archive=adult-only (>=18y); v1.0 mixed scope (includes newborn 0-28d 25,018 cells + postnatal/children/adolescents) retained in donor_level_adult_pool_contrast (tier=...__adult_pool__v1.0). FALLBACK_BLOCKED guard implemented (triggers prohibition on fallback when tissue group has 0 adult donors) —— This empirical test triggered 0 layers, each tissue group adult-only has real support.",
  "t_e1febb8e (2026-09-24) addition: Corneal stromal keratocyte reference grid —— Among D002 adult primary archive 67 donor units, existing author-labeled Corneal Stromal Keratocytes class units have pooled ~23.4% (unit median ~20%; mixed ocular surface captured event scope, not pure cornea ground truth, not compliance line); literature range grid=missing item falls to blocked (see stromal_keratocyte_reference); marker library corneal two-class supplementary recording and hierarchy mapping see markers library v1-membrane-20260924 and concept entries EYEKBC-0018/0019."
 ],
